  "title": "Adopted Building Codes | Castle Rock, CO - Official Website",
  "text": "Adopted Building Codes | Castle Rock, CO - Official Website\nSkip to Main Content\nEmail scam alert\nReported email scam targeting Town of Castle Rock eTRAKiT system applicants\nRead On...\nAnnexation\nBuilding\nFee Schedule\nHomeowner Resources\nPlanning\nZoning\nSearch\nHome\nTown Government\nDepartments and Divisions\nDevelopment Services\nBuilding\nAdopted Building Codes\nAdopted Building Codes\nBuilding and wildfire codes take effect this summer\nBuilding Codes - Adopted amendments to the Town of Castle Rock Building Codes took effect June 30, 2026. The 2025 Colorado Wildfire Resiliency Code took effect July 1, 2026.\nBuilding codes promote safety\nThe Town of Castle Rock has adopted the following building and fire codes for all new permit submittals.\nSee Title 15 of the\nMunicipal Code\nfor any specific exceptions to these codes adopted by the Town of Castle Rock.\n2024 International Building Code\n2024 International Residential Code\n2024 International Plumbing Code\n2024 International Mechanical Code\n2021 International Energy Conservation Code\n2024 International Fuel Gas Code\n2024 International Fire Code\n2024 International Existing Building Code\n2024 International Swimming Pool and Spa Code\n2017 ANSI A117.1\n1997 Uniform Code for the Abatement of Dangerous Buildings\n2026 National Electrical Code\nASME A17.1 2022 Elevator Code\nASME A18.1 2020 Safety Standard for Platform Lifts and Stairway Chairlifts\nASME A17.3 2023 Safety Code for Existing Elevators and Escalators\nASCE 21, Parts 1 through 4 Automated People Mover Standards\n2025 Colorado Wildfire Resiliency Code\nModel Colorado Electric Ready and Solar Ready Code\nThe subject matter of the codes concerns regulations to provide minimum standards to safeguard life or limb, property and public welfare by regulating and controlling:\nDesign\nConstruction and quality of materials\nUse and Occupancy\nLocation and maintenance of all buildings, structures, plumbing systems and mechanical systems in the Town\nAdopted Building Codes\nBoard of Building Appeals\nBuilding Inspections\nBuilding Reports\nBuilding Use Tax\nCommercial Permits\nAdopted Building Codes\nContractor Registration\nInspections\nContractor Luncheons\nContractor Registration\nEconomic Development Assistance\nElevators and Conveyances\nRe-Roof Checklist\nResidential Decks and Patios\nResidential Permits\nAdopted Building Codes\nContractor Registration\nInspections\nSigns\nAccess Online Services\nApply for Jobs\nAttend an Event\nPay Water Bill\nTrack Roadwork\nView Development Activity\nContact Us\n100 N. Wilcox St.\nCastle Rock, CO 80104\nPhone:\n720-896-8696\nTown staff directory\nTown news sign up\nConnect With Us\nFacebook\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nNextdoor\nX\nYouTube\nHelpful Links\nAccess online services\nFact or Fiction?\nFrequently asked questions\nLocal business directory\nTown amenities\nAdmin login\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nHome\nParks & Rec\nWater\nPolice\nFire\nPublic Works\nDevelopment\nAccessibility\nCopyright\nNondiscrimination\nPrivacy\nSite Map\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by\nCivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nArrow Left\nArrow Right\n[]\nSlideshow Left Arrow\nSlideshow Right Arrow",
